WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.074
This tutorial builds a five second animated intro in the VideoForge Studio.

2
00:00:06.074 --> 00:00:12.391
It contains a headline, an accent bar, a tagline, a floating badge and a lower third.

3
00:00:12.391 --> 00:00:17.890
No footage is required, and the whole project takes about fifteen minutes.

4
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.570
Begin by naming the project.

5
00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:25.053
Select the project name at the top left and enter Animated intro.

6
00:00:25.053 --> 00:00:30.363
With nothing selected, the inspector on the right shows the project settings.

7
00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:33.190
Set the background colour to a deep navy.

8
00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.570
Now add the headline.

9
00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:40.510
Choose Add title, and type the headline text into the inspector.

10
00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:49.387
Set the size to ten percent, select Poppins in bold, and raise the title to forty four percent of the frame height.

11
00:00:49.387 --> 00:00:52.860
Finally, extend its duration to five seconds.

12
00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:56.966
Open the Motion tab and expand Motion presets.

13
00:00:56.966 --> 00:01:01.986
Set the preset duration to zero point nine seconds and select Spring.

14
00:01:01.986 --> 00:01:04.314
Press play to review the result.

15
00:01:04.314 --> 00:01:09.770
The headline arrives with a controlled bounce, and then settles into place.

16
00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:12.407
Next, add an accent bar.

17
00:01:12.407 --> 00:01:16.104
Open the Graphics panel and insert a rectangle.

18
00:01:16.104 --> 00:01:24.126
Reduce its height to a thin line, fill it with the brand orange, and position it beneath the headline.

19
00:01:24.126 --> 00:01:29.710
Then apply the Wipe reveal preset, so the bar opens from left to right.

20
00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:38.781
Add a tagline in the same way.

21
00:01:38.781 --> 00:01:42.510
Insert a second title and enter the supporting text.

22
00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:48.318
Reduce the size, and choose a softer colour, so that it ranks below the headline.

23
00:01:48.318 --> 00:01:52.620
Apply the Rise preset, and the tagline climbs into position.

24
00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:02.619
The badge should keep moving for the whole intro.

25
00:02:02.619 --> 00:02:07.629
Insert an ellipse from the Graphics panel and size it as a small circle.

26
00:02:07.629 --> 00:02:13.335
In the Motion tab, expand Animate with code, choose the Float recipe and apply it.

27
00:02:13.335 --> 00:02:17.440
The motion comes from a formula, so it loops at any length.

28
00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:24.759
Move the playhead to two seconds, then open the Lower third template in the Graphics panel.

29
00:02:24.759 --> 00:02:31.080
Enter a name and a supporting line, set the duration to three seconds, and add it to the timeline.

30
00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.240
It appears exactly where the playhead was placed.

31
00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:40.529
To refine the motion, switch to the Animate workspace and select the headline.

32
00:02:40.529 --> 00:02:43.440
Each animated property has its own curve.

33
00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:48.057
Add a keyframe at the playhead, and drag it to adjust the timing.

34
00:02:48.057 --> 00:02:51.820
When you have finished, return to the Edit workspace.

35
00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:54.089
Now soften the ending.

36
00:02:54.089 --> 00:02:58.441
Select the headline and set Fade out to zero point six seconds.

37
00:02:58.441 --> 00:03:03.760
Repeat this for the tagline, so that both elements leave the screen together.

38
00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:10.882
Before exporting, open the project settings and choose Fit everything.

39
00:03:10.882 --> 00:03:14.609
This confirms that every layer sits inside the frame.

40
00:03:14.609 --> 00:03:19.390
Return to the start of the timeline and play the full sequence once.

41
00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:25.265
Finally, select Export.

42
00:03:25.265 --> 00:03:32.564
The render runs on the server with FFmpeg, and the progress panel reports each stage.

43
00:03:32.564 --> 00:03:36.600
When it finishes, the MP4 is ready to download.

44
00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.973
That completes the animated intro.

45
00:03:39.973 --> 00:03:46.377
Every layer is an ordinary clip, so you can retime or restyle any part at any time.

46
00:03:46.377 --> 00:03:52.780
The next tutorial introduces the Animator, which lets you rig and pose a character.

